# Generated by StepForge — by Md Zarin Tasnim · Prepared by Md Zarin Tasnim · 2026-10-07
Feature: API
  Shop Desk, Staging environment.

  @api @p2
  Scenario: Orders API
    When send POST /oauth/token (save as token)
    Then status is 200
    When send POST /api/{{env.api-version}}/orders (save as order)
    Then status is 201 and $.id exists and $.items[*].sku contains "A-1" and header:content-type contains "json" and time is at most 800 and $.total inRange [0,1000] and $ matchesSchema {"type":"object"}
    When read the location header of the response (save as location)
    And read the response status (save as code)
    And send GET /admin
    And send GET /reports
    And send DELETE /api/orders/{{vars.order.id}}
    And send GET /me
    And send GET /x
    Then status is 200
    When send POST /files
    And send PUT https://other.test/raw
    And send a GraphQL query to /graphql
    Then $.data.me.id is not empty
    When if {{vars.code}} equals "201"
    And note: Created {{vars.order.id}}
    # Otherwise:
    And note: Not created
    And repeat 3 times
    And send GET /ping?i={{vars.index}}
    And repeat for each line in {{vars.order.items}}
    And note: {{vars.line.sku}}
    And repeat while the "Load more" button is visible
    And note: more
    And if "Out of stock" is on the page
    And note: oos
    And repeat while {{vars.index}} lt "3"
    And send GET /poll
    And remember "[object Object]" as payload
    And generate a random pattern (save as ref)
    And generate a random date (save as due)
    And wait 250 ms
    And run a script (save as double)

  @api @p2
  Scenario: Integrations
    When call the SOAP service /soap/prices (urn:GetPrice) (save as price)
    Then status is 200 and //p:Price is above 0 and count(//p:Line) is at least 1
    When call the SOAP service https://soap.example.test/ws (urn:Ping)
    Then xpath://*[local-name()="Pong"] exists
    When send a Kafka message to orders with key "{{vars.ref}}"
    Then offset exists
    When wait for a Kafka message on invoices where $.orderId is "{{vars.ref}}" (save as invoice)
    Then $.status is "issued" and header:source is "billing"
    When upload /in/prices-{{run.id}}.csv on SFTP files.shop.test
    And download /out/report.csv on FTP files.shop.test (save as report)
    Then content contains "A-1"
    When list /in on FTPS files.shop.test
    Then count is at least 1
